      \field{abstract}{Accurate turning is not an easy task for the quadruped robot and previous work mainly addresses the problem with complex control strategy or systems. This paper proposes a design method for the accurate turning motion of a quadruped robot with 12 degrees of freedom (DOF). Unlike others, we have achieved precise turning motion with a relatively simple geometric approach. Once the parameters of desired movement are set, such as the turning radius and angles, the robot can realize corresponding circle locomotion. A design architecture including geometric analysis, 3D foot trajectory design and inverse kinematics is presented to solve the problem systematically. In addition, according to the different conditions, the corresponding compensation coefﬁcient is necessarily considered in order to acquire precise values of leg joints. At last, comparison results by several experiments have identiﬁed the feasibility and accuracy of turning along a circle trajectory based on our proposed method.}
