      \field{abstract}{Actuator saturation is a fundamental nonlinearity that significantly degrades the performance of PID-controlled systems by inducing integrator windup, causing overshoot, slow recovery, and even instability. This paper presents a comparative analysis of classical and advanced anti-windup techniques for PI-controlled first-order-plus-dead-time processes, including back-calculation (dynamic and instantaneous), conditional integration, and hybrid approaches, and proposes a novel hybrid strategy combining conditional integration with dynamic back-calculation together with systematic tuning rules for the tracking time constant.}
